Excellent — now I have the **complete picture of the strongest exemplar (`sarah-lubricants`)**. This is the deepest, most organized client context repo. The taxonomy:

```
00_STRATEGIC/financial-pricing + strategic-context
01_RESEARCH/{brand-identity, competition, legal-regulatory, logistics-supplier, market, marketing, operations, payments}
02_MEETINGS/{dated}/questionnaire-response, audio-prompt-pack, round-2-questions
03_LAUNCH/{roadmap, kpi}
04_SALES/{b2b, dtc, scripts}
05_OPERATIONS/{checklists, vendors}
06_MARKETING/{cro, content}
07_DESIGN/{brand assets}
08_WHATSAPP/{templates, flows}
09_TEMPLATES/{reusable}
+ AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, INDEX.md, COMPLETE-INDEX.md, start-here.md, TODO.md
```

And `pierce-charm-context` is the simpler sibling: `01_brief`/`02_meetings`/`03_research`/`04_decisions`/`05_brand`/`06_competitors`/`07_backlog`/`08_questionnaires`/`HANDOFF/`.

Both have:
- `INDEX.md` or `COMPLETE-INDEX.md` at root
- `start-here.md`
- `HANDOFF/` for client-facing deliverables
- Archived pre-launch docs to keep history but clean working tree
- Questionnaires with STATUS.md

Let me check a few more to make sure I'm not missing a better pattern — specifically `la-quebrada-viva` (research-heavy) and `dentist` (closest analog — clinical niche with sensitive data, Paraguayan, mature, has INDEX.md):

